WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:01.383
- Welcome.
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.383 --> 00:00:03.720
I hugged y'all earlier so
y'all didn't have to get up.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.180
So it's nice to meet y'all, all of you.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.013
I've never met any of you.

00:00:07.013 --> 00:00:09.120
So is this the first
time you're back together

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.677
since shooting the movie?

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.300
- We did. Key West.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.591
- No, we got to go to Key West.

00:00:13.591 --> 00:00:14.873
- Yeah, we did some (indistinct) together.

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:15.706
- They came to Key West.

00:00:15.706 --> 00:00:16.666
- A few weeks ago.

00:00:16.666 --> 00:00:17.499
- My hometown.

00:00:17.499 --> 00:00:18.332
- [Kelly] Oh, so you got to-

00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:19.898
- And we did a wonderful screening there.

00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:21.236
- A whole screening there. That's awesome.

00:00:21.236 --> 00:00:22.069
- Yeah.

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:22.912
- Judy has a bookstore there.

00:00:22.912 --> 00:00:23.745
- Yeah.

00:00:23.745 --> 00:00:27.472
- And a theater that she
built from the ground up.

00:00:27.472 --> 00:00:28.878
Not with her own bare hands.

00:00:28.878 --> 00:00:29.711
- That's exciting.

00:00:29.711 --> 00:00:30.544
- [Rachel] But, you know (indistinct).

00:00:30.544 --> 00:00:31.678
- You would be so multi-talented

00:00:31.678 --> 00:00:33.178
if you built the theater yourself.

00:00:33.178 --> 00:00:34.298
- I'm sorry. I did not.

00:00:34.298 --> 00:00:35.385
- No, that's incredible.

00:00:35.385 --> 00:00:36.322
Was that important to you?

00:00:36.322 --> 00:00:38.652
To be able to give back to the community?

00:00:38.652 --> 00:00:39.485
- It was wonderful.

00:00:39.485 --> 00:00:40.318
- [Kelly] It's wonderful.

00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:41.965
- I mean, this event was
giving to the community.

00:00:41.965 --> 00:00:43.577
- Yeah. But I just mean
the theater in general.

00:00:43.577 --> 00:00:44.952
That's cool. The bookstore.

00:00:44.952 --> 00:00:45.785
- [Judy] Yeah.

00:00:45.785 --> 00:00:46.738
- That's awesome for a community to have

00:00:46.738 --> 00:00:48.736
that kind of like vibe,

00:00:48.736 --> 00:00:50.569
like just to where you
could come together.

00:00:50.569 --> 00:00:51.658
I love that you did that.

00:00:51.658 --> 00:00:53.465
So we have to start with the story.

00:00:53.465 --> 00:00:56.278
So you published this in 1970.

00:00:56.278 --> 00:00:58.485
So did you feel then that it was something

00:00:58.485 --> 00:00:59.526
that was gonna take off like it did,

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.706
or were you just doing you?

00:01:01.706 --> 00:01:02.959
- You have to be kidding, like,

00:01:02.959 --> 00:01:05.093
I didn't know what I
was doing, let alone...

00:01:05.093 --> 00:01:05.937
- You had no idea?

00:01:05.937 --> 00:01:06.770
- No.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:07.626
- That's hilarious.

00:01:07.626 --> 00:01:09.685
- I had no idea. I just let it out.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:12.184
- Yeah. 50 years later we're
still talking about it.

00:01:12.184 --> 00:01:13.017
- And here it is.

00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:14.466
- That's incredible.

00:01:14.466 --> 00:01:16.186
So what were your
experiences with the book?

00:01:16.186 --> 00:01:17.080
You're very young.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.086
So did you read this for the movie?

00:01:19.086 --> 00:01:20.010
Or had you already read?

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.706
- I actually hadn't read it before.

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:22.539
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:22.539 --> 00:01:24.226
- I got the audition for it,
but as soon as I read the book

00:01:24.226 --> 00:01:27.032
I remember going to my parents
and I was like, oh my gosh,

00:01:27.032 --> 00:01:29.583
how did someone write
down this experience?

00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:30.416
This is it.

00:01:30.416 --> 00:01:31.249
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:31.249 --> 00:01:32.082
- How did someone write this down?

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:32.915
Oh, and it's all a credit to you.

00:01:32.915 --> 00:01:34.566
- 'Cause you're like there,
you're experiencing it.

00:01:34.566 --> 00:01:35.399
Yeah.

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:38.378
- Yeah. And I, as soon as I
started the audition process

00:01:38.378 --> 00:01:39.840
and started filming, I was going through

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.497
the exact same stuff that Margaret was.

00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:42.340
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.603
- Like at the exact same time
that I was shooting the movie.

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:46.437
So I think it came for me at
the perfect time in my life.

00:01:46.437 --> 00:01:47.270
- Yeah.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.331
- Because I could draw on a lot of my own

00:01:48.331 --> 00:01:50.718
awkward, messy, weird experiences

00:01:50.718 --> 00:01:53.185
as I was exploring
Margaret's character as well.

00:01:53.185 --> 00:01:54.766
- Yeah. Puberty is rough.

00:01:54.766 --> 00:01:55.599
(guests laughing)

00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:57.393
Rach, it was not great for me.

00:01:57.393 --> 00:01:59.017
What about you?

00:01:59.017 --> 00:02:00.746
Did you read this when you were younger?

00:02:00.746 --> 00:02:01.598
- I didn't.

00:02:01.598 --> 00:02:03.146
I read a lot of Judy's stuff.

00:02:03.146 --> 00:02:04.646
I love the Fudge series.

00:02:04.646 --> 00:02:06.433
I read a lot of her
books when I was younger,

00:02:06.433 --> 00:02:09.233
but I hadn't read Margaret.

00:02:09.233 --> 00:02:12.457
I was like, oh, this about
boobs and things like,

00:02:12.457 --> 00:02:13.559
(Judy laughing)

00:02:13.559 --> 00:02:15.798
and I think I was seven when
it came on my radar, you know?

00:02:15.798 --> 00:02:16.631
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:16.631 --> 00:02:18.546
- All my friend's older
sisters who were like 10

00:02:18.546 --> 00:02:21.986
were reading it and I
was like, oh one day.

00:02:21.986 --> 00:02:25.246
I didn't realize I would be
like 40 when that one day came.

00:02:25.246 --> 00:02:26.079
(Judy laughing)

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:26.912
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:28.712
- And I'd be playing
Margaret's mom, you know?

00:02:28.712 --> 00:02:30.206
I mean, that's just still blows my mind.

00:02:30.206 --> 00:02:31.286
Thank you so much.

00:02:31.286 --> 00:02:32.360
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.439
- I love it.

00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:34.371
- So when I-

00:02:34.371 --> 00:02:35.204
- It's such a pop culture thing. Yeah.

00:02:35.204 --> 00:02:36.037
- It really is.

00:02:36.037 --> 00:02:40.080
So when I did finally read
it for the film, you know,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.753
there were so many great nuggets
for my character in there

00:02:42.753 --> 00:02:45.672
and it was great to read it as
a mom about to play this mom.

00:02:45.672 --> 00:02:47.926
But what I also loved is that

00:02:47.926 --> 00:02:50.278
I related so much to Margaret, you know.

00:02:50.278 --> 00:02:52.612
I was like, oh, I see why this is such

00:02:52.612 --> 00:02:53.445
- [Kelly] Mm-hmm.

00:02:53.445 --> 00:02:54.453
- a timeless story.

00:02:54.453 --> 00:02:57.560
I just went right back to my childhood

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.173
in all the feels and-

00:02:59.173 --> 00:03:00.006
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:00.006 --> 00:03:02.893
- And yeah, it just really packed a punch.

00:03:02.893 --> 00:03:05.057
- Yeah. A lot of things change in life.

00:03:05.057 --> 00:03:05.890
Not puberty.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:06.723
- Nope.

00:03:06.723 --> 00:03:07.556
(everyone laughing)

00:03:07.556 --> 00:03:08.573
- Just sucks at any generation.

00:03:08.573 --> 00:03:09.953
It's just hard.

00:03:09.953 --> 00:03:11.664
But you've played moms before,

00:03:11.664 --> 00:03:13.503
but now you're a mom playing a mom.

00:03:13.503 --> 00:03:14.336
Was that different for you?

00:03:14.336 --> 00:03:17.166
- Yeah, I think I was
more relaxed about it.

00:03:17.166 --> 00:03:18.412
I was always worried-

00:03:18.412 --> 00:03:19.477
- Put more pressure when
you didn't have kids.

00:03:19.477 --> 00:03:20.310
Am I doing this right?

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.646
- didn't have kids when
I was playing moms.

00:03:21.646 --> 00:03:24.599
I was like, oh, I'm missing
something, I'm sure of it.

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:26.165
You know, it's like,

00:03:26.165 --> 00:03:28.799
your idea of being a mom is so different

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:29.632
from the real thing.

00:03:29.632 --> 00:03:30.465
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:30.465 --> 00:03:31.298
- So yeah.

00:03:31.298 --> 00:03:35.043
I think I didn't do as much
mom research. (laughing)

00:03:35.043 --> 00:03:35.876
- Yeah.

00:03:35.876 --> 00:03:37.120
Well, I think when you
figure out you are mom,

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.757
no one's got it figured out, so.

00:03:38.757 --> 00:03:39.906
- Right. Exactly.

00:03:39.906 --> 00:03:41.766
Yeah. It's a crapshoot.

00:03:41.766 --> 00:03:43.066
Just get out there and try.

00:03:43.066 --> 00:03:45.459
- (laughing) Try, try your best.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:47.286
Go for that green participation ribbon.

00:03:47.286 --> 00:03:50.100
So did you have a hand in the casting?

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.810
- I did the whole thing.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:52.800
No, no, I'm kidding.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.457
No. You know, casting
belonged to the director.

00:03:55.457 --> 00:03:56.386
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:56.386 --> 00:04:00.426
- Really, and Kelly and I
developed a wonderful relationship

00:04:00.426 --> 00:04:01.259
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:01.259 --> 00:04:02.833
- And a wonderful working relationship.

00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:04.453
But casting was hers.

00:04:04.453 --> 00:04:09.206
But she would send me tapes
and when she found Margaret,

00:04:09.206 --> 00:04:12.352
she knew instantly that
she found Margaret.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:13.185
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:15.824
And she told me, she said,

00:04:15.824 --> 00:04:17.493
I don't want to embarrass you.

00:04:17.493 --> 00:04:21.966
I'm sending you this
tape. And she is Margaret.

00:04:21.966 --> 00:04:22.799
- [Kelly] Oh, I love it.

00:04:22.799 --> 00:04:23.632
- And she was Margaret.

00:04:23.632 --> 00:04:24.465
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:24.465 --> 00:04:25.298
- And she is Margaret.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:26.131
- Aw.

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:26.964
- [Kelly] Do you feel like-

00:04:26.964 --> 00:04:27.797
- Which is me, you know,

00:04:27.797 --> 00:04:28.665
because I'm Margaret.
- I know, I was gonna say,

00:04:28.665 --> 00:04:29.940
is that the character in the story

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.786
that you relate to, like still?

00:04:31.786 --> 00:04:33.646
Is that the one you kind
of relate to the most?

00:04:33.646 --> 00:04:34.479
- Totally.
- Yeah.

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:35.312
- I am Margaret.

00:04:35.312 --> 00:04:36.145
- Yeah.

00:04:36.145 --> 00:04:36.978
- I mean, I was Margaret.

00:04:36.978 --> 00:04:37.811
- Yeah.

00:04:37.811 --> 00:04:38.644
- Not totally.

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:39.477
- It wasn't like a biography,
but yes, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:39.477 --> 00:04:40.310
- No, no, not totally.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:41.143
- Yeah.

00:04:41.143 --> 00:04:43.786
- But, you know, I mean,
that's the girl I was.

00:04:43.786 --> 00:04:45.143
- Yeah.

00:04:45.143 --> 00:04:47.058
- But so many of the
things I would tell kids

00:04:47.058 --> 00:04:49.479
when they asked me about
Margaret, I would say,

00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:51.144
well now you know my secrets.

00:04:51.144 --> 00:04:52.478
- (laughing) Yeah. It's all out there.

00:04:52.478 --> 00:04:53.693
(guests laughing)

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:54.526
- Some of them anyway.

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:57.999
- I have always been
amazed with how well Rachel

00:04:57.999 --> 00:05:00.606
cries and talks at the
same time in movies.

00:05:00.606 --> 00:05:01.439
(Rachel laughing)

00:05:01.439 --> 00:05:02.272
This is not a joke.

00:05:02.272 --> 00:05:03.105
(audience laughing)

00:05:03.105 --> 00:05:04.080
I'm not just saying
- (indistinct)

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.626
- this right now.

00:05:05.626 --> 00:05:08.083
I, just on this show alone, we have proof,

00:05:08.083 --> 00:05:10.153
but I've said it many a times in life.

00:05:10.153 --> 00:05:12.151
Here's the tape.

00:05:12.151 --> 00:05:14.433
I wish I could like Rachel
McAdams cry from The Notebook,

00:05:14.433 --> 00:05:16.058
but it's just not in the cards.

00:05:16.058 --> 00:05:16.933
- It's not reality.

00:05:16.933 --> 00:05:17.766
- Yeah.

00:05:17.766 --> 00:05:18.599
- It's not.

00:05:18.599 --> 00:05:19.432
- That's not real.

00:05:19.432 --> 00:05:20.265
I just need a minute. I'm so sorry.

00:05:20.265 --> 00:05:22.251
I can't talk when I cry. I'm
not Rachel McAdams. (sniffling)

00:05:22.251 --> 00:05:24.761
(everyone laughing)

00:05:24.761 --> 00:05:26.178
I can't, I can't.

00:05:27.871 --> 00:05:28.704
- You look good.

00:05:28.704 --> 00:05:29.537
- Yeah, totally.

00:05:29.537 --> 00:05:30.370
- Nothing is dripping.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:31.353
- Not everyone looks great crying.

00:05:31.353 --> 00:05:32.380
- You don't look like Giuliani at all.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.755
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:34.755 --> 00:05:37.188
- I also don't look like Rachel
McAdams from The Notebook.

00:05:37.188 --> 00:05:38.293
So I'm trying to handle it.

00:05:38.293 --> 00:05:39.302
(everyone laughing)

00:05:39.302 --> 00:05:40.135
(wind whooshing)

00:05:40.135 --> 00:05:40.968
(audience cheering)

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:41.801
- I'm not kidding.

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:42.988
I say it all the-

00:05:42.988 --> 00:05:43.821
- (laughing) Oh my god.

00:05:43.821 --> 00:05:46.240
- Because you know what
it is? I'm angry about it.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.073
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:47.073 --> 00:05:49.635
Like, I don't understand how you do that.

00:05:49.635 --> 00:05:50.468
(Rachel laughing)

00:05:50.468 --> 00:05:52.833
Like, you have this thing where you cry

00:05:52.833 --> 00:05:56.189
and still look beautiful and it's gross.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.375
It's like what?

00:05:57.375 --> 00:05:58.739
- It's so disgusting.

00:05:58.739 --> 00:06:02.626
- Like your ugly cry is still
unbelievably cute and sexy.

00:06:02.626 --> 00:06:03.459
I don't get it.

00:06:03.459 --> 00:06:04.292
(Rachel laughing)

00:06:04.292 --> 00:06:05.486
What are you, why?

00:06:05.486 --> 00:06:07.209
Like how do you do that?

00:06:07.209 --> 00:06:09.126
How do you hold your face together?

00:06:09.126 --> 00:06:10.126
- I practice

00:06:11.546 --> 00:06:12.986
(Kelly laughing)

00:06:12.986 --> 00:06:14.166
in front of a mirror.

00:06:14.166 --> 00:06:14.999
- Okay.

00:06:14.999 --> 00:06:15.895
- For a really long time.

00:06:15.895 --> 00:06:16.728
- Okay.

00:06:16.728 --> 00:06:19.592
- No, I'm teaching a Masterclass in-

00:06:19.592 --> 00:06:20.622
- (laughing) Crying

00:06:20.622 --> 00:06:21.955
- Pretty crying.

00:06:22.805 --> 00:06:25.473
I don't know. I don't feel
like it is pretty, but-

00:06:25.473 --> 00:06:26.600
- Oh my God.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:27.593
- And I think you look gorgeous.

00:06:27.593 --> 00:06:28.426
- It's adorable.

00:06:28.426 --> 00:06:29.793
You're lying. And I love you for it.

00:06:29.793 --> 00:06:31.066
(audience laughing)

00:06:31.066 --> 00:06:32.526
It's just one of those things
I was like, oh my gosh,

00:06:32.526 --> 00:06:33.860
she comes on here, we
have to talk about this.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.566
It's literally, I say it everywhere.

00:06:35.566 --> 00:06:37.090
- [Rachel] That's so funny.

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.998
- Because it's one of those
things I feel like is rare.

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.986
Even like the greatest
actors think about movie.

00:06:40.986 --> 00:06:42.659
You're like, not everybody
looks great crying

00:06:42.659 --> 00:06:46.799
- But if you grew up watching
Demi Moore in Ghosts.

00:06:46.799 --> 00:06:47.632
- Oh, I did.

00:06:47.632 --> 00:06:49.866
- You know, that tear
- [Kelly] The one tear.

00:06:49.866 --> 00:06:51.184
- here where
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:51.184 --> 00:06:52.017
- nothing else is moving.

00:06:52.017 --> 00:06:52.973
Like the act-, you know,
that's an actress's,

00:06:52.973 --> 00:06:53.806
Like, oh,

00:06:53.806 --> 00:06:54.639
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:54.639 --> 00:06:55.472
- if I can get that to Mecca.

00:06:55.472 --> 00:06:56.360
- Don't worry. You're there.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:59.384
Yeah. It's upsetting to the rest of us.

00:06:59.384 --> 00:07:00.222
(Rachel laughing)

00:07:00.222 --> 00:07:02.484
It's like, wait, I look like a hot mess.

00:07:02.484 --> 00:07:04.404
Like, is she all right?

00:07:04.404 --> 00:07:06.137
Like, that's how I look, anyway.

00:07:06.137 --> 00:07:06.970
(audience applauding)

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:07.803
So Rachel, do you remember going through

00:07:07.803 --> 00:07:09.761
those adolescent moments
that, I don't know,

00:07:09.761 --> 00:07:11.594
Margaret goes through it in the movie?

00:07:11.594 --> 00:07:13.357
You still, I mean, I know the
trauma is still kind of there.

00:07:13.357 --> 00:07:14.377
- Yeah, it's fresh.

00:07:14.377 --> 00:07:16.197
- Like I just, I had, let me tell you,

00:07:16.197 --> 00:07:18.030
braces, glasses, acne.

00:07:19.115 --> 00:07:23.061
Like literally everything
that could go wrong

00:07:23.061 --> 00:07:24.697
was happening with me.

00:07:24.697 --> 00:07:25.530
- [Rachel] Right.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:26.363
- Like, did you?

00:07:26.363 --> 00:07:28.207
Just lie to me and tell
me you had that existence?

00:07:28.207 --> 00:07:29.617
(Rachel laughing)

00:07:29.617 --> 00:07:31.734
Like, don't say it was perfect.

00:07:31.734 --> 00:07:33.244
I will throw this pillow at you.

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:35.374
(hand thudding)

00:07:35.374 --> 00:07:37.733
- Nope. Definitely far from perfect.

00:07:37.733 --> 00:07:39.150
Yeah. So awkward.

00:07:40.117 --> 00:07:42.713
And am I normal? Am I like everyone else?

00:07:42.713 --> 00:07:43.546
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:43.546 --> 00:07:46.786
- You know, just hair, so much hair drama.

00:07:46.786 --> 00:07:49.893
I chopped all my hair off
when I was in grade seven

00:07:49.893 --> 00:07:52.646
and I would spend hours every morning

00:07:52.646 --> 00:07:54.871
trying to make it work.

00:07:54.871 --> 00:07:55.704
- Yeah.

00:07:55.704 --> 00:07:58.150
- And then I'd walk to school
in a blizzard in Canada

00:07:58.150 --> 00:08:00.043
and it would be like
(raspberry blowing), you know?

00:08:00.043 --> 00:08:00.959
- Bobby pins.

00:08:00.959 --> 00:08:02.339
- Bobby pins. You needed bobby pins.

00:08:02.339 --> 00:08:07.064
This is a joke because an
early line in the book.

00:08:07.064 --> 00:08:07.897
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:07.897 --> 00:08:09.132
- Margaret's trying to hold her hair up.

00:08:09.132 --> 00:08:10.513
She's letting it grow back.

00:08:10.513 --> 00:08:11.576
It was, she cut it.

00:08:11.576 --> 00:08:12.409
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:12.409 --> 00:08:13.516
- And it's the bobby pins.

00:08:13.516 --> 00:08:14.703
- Bobby pins.

00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:16.579
And then when I started seeing the cuts,

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:18.233
it's like, oh my God.

00:08:18.233 --> 00:08:19.066
They never-

00:08:19.066 --> 00:08:20.013
- Bobby pins everywhere.

00:08:20.013 --> 00:08:21.245
- They never take-
- Always in my hair.

00:08:21.245 --> 00:08:22.879
- the bobby pins out of her hair.

00:08:22.879 --> 00:08:24.444
- We had to meticulously place them

00:08:24.444 --> 00:08:27.699
in the exact same spot
every single day on set.

00:08:27.699 --> 00:08:28.532
- Oh my gosh.

00:08:28.532 --> 00:08:29.473
- [Judy] She has bobby pins-

00:08:29.473 --> 00:08:30.306
- Continuity. Wow.

00:08:30.306 --> 00:08:33.146
- Continuity. Yeah. It was insane.

00:08:33.146 --> 00:08:34.537
- That's hard.

00:08:34.537 --> 00:08:37.723
But Abby how do you think social
media affects all of this?

00:08:37.723 --> 00:08:39.433
'Cause we didn't grow up in that. Like-

00:08:39.433 --> 00:08:40.553
- Yeah, honestly...

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:41.705
- You know, that came out later for us.

00:08:41.705 --> 00:08:44.659
- I think it does have a big influence

00:08:44.659 --> 00:08:46.205
on these conversations.

00:08:46.205 --> 00:08:47.038
It does.

00:08:47.038 --> 00:08:49.243
Because we see, every single day,

00:08:49.243 --> 00:08:52.036
we see all of these people and images

00:08:52.036 --> 00:08:55.910
that are kind of falsified
in planting false information

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.051
in our brains and like creating a standard

00:08:58.051 --> 00:09:00.266
that we're never gonna
be able to live up to.

00:09:00.266 --> 00:09:03.159
And I think that, especially
at this time where

00:09:03.159 --> 00:09:06.163
we have social media and
also the conversation

00:09:06.163 --> 00:09:09.199
around periods and boobs
and bras and all this stuff

00:09:09.199 --> 00:09:11.606
is kind of being censored in a way.

00:09:11.606 --> 00:09:12.439
- [Kelly] Hmm.

00:09:12.439 --> 00:09:14.619
- And I think we really need
to have these conversations

00:09:14.619 --> 00:09:17.016
because it's super important
that we talk about this

00:09:17.016 --> 00:09:18.533
because a lot of people go through it.

00:09:18.533 --> 00:09:20.638
And it's important to
know that you're not alone

00:09:20.638 --> 00:09:23.066
and it's important to
have actual information.

00:09:23.066 --> 00:09:23.899
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:09:23.899 --> 00:09:24.732
- That is-

00:09:24.732 --> 00:09:25.565
- [Kelly] The correct information.

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:28.119
- the correct information. Yeah. And-

00:09:28.119 --> 00:09:29.220
- I learned on a school bus.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.053
- [Abby] Oh God.

00:09:30.053 --> 00:09:31.765
- It was not correct.

00:09:31.765 --> 00:09:33.079
(everyone laughing)

00:09:33.079 --> 00:09:35.453
It was kinda' weird.

00:09:35.453 --> 00:09:37.913
So Rachel, when you were
just a little younger

00:09:37.913 --> 00:09:39.703
than Margaret, you wanted to
be a professional ice skater,

00:09:39.703 --> 00:09:40.716
which I did not know.

00:09:40.716 --> 00:09:42.059
- Yeah.

00:09:42.059 --> 00:09:42.892
- Wow.

00:09:42.892 --> 00:09:44.619
- For a second. For a second.

00:09:44.619 --> 00:09:45.452
- I had to bring it up.

00:09:45.452 --> 00:09:47.006
I was like, that's like
something we all dreamed

00:09:47.006 --> 00:09:48.723
but never actually did.

00:09:48.723 --> 00:09:50.104
Like, but you did.
- I didn't do it either.

00:09:50.104 --> 00:09:51.038
- [Kelly] Yeah. You were skating.

00:09:51.038 --> 00:09:51.871
- I was a skater.

00:09:51.871 --> 00:09:52.704
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:09:52.704 --> 00:09:53.750
- Yes. I wasn't very
professional, but yes,

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:54.586
I was a skater.

00:09:54.586 --> 00:09:56.019
I skated from four to 17

00:09:56.019 --> 00:09:56.852
(audience cooing)

00:09:56.852 --> 00:09:57.766
until I went to theater school.

00:09:57.766 --> 00:09:59.526
- That's a skater. Four to 17.

00:09:59.526 --> 00:10:01.586
I'm like, I did it like once a year

00:10:01.586 --> 00:10:03.370
with all my friends and we fell down.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:04.703
Like nobody actually ever did it.

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:05.536
- [Rachel] Right.

00:10:05.536 --> 00:10:07.333
- Did you actually have a real dream

00:10:07.333 --> 00:10:09.346
of wanting to do it professionally?

00:10:09.346 --> 00:10:11.006
- I did for a time. Yeah. Yeah.

00:10:11.006 --> 00:10:11.839
- [Kelly] Yeah?

00:10:11.839 --> 00:10:12.672
- When I was younger. Yeah.

00:10:12.672 --> 00:10:14.159
And funny enough, I hit puberty

00:10:14.159 --> 00:10:16.992
and everything goes somewhere and-

00:10:18.412 --> 00:10:19.245
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:19.245 --> 00:10:21.473
- You know, it's like doing
jumps was like (groaning).

00:10:21.473 --> 00:10:22.859
- Yeah. Well those are hips.

00:10:22.859 --> 00:10:24.866
- When I'm swinging myself
around the ice the way I was.

00:10:24.866 --> 00:10:25.751
Yeah. But-

00:10:25.751 --> 00:10:26.584
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:26.584 --> 00:10:29.184
- but no, you know, to become a, you know,

00:10:29.184 --> 00:10:31.586
a champion ice skater, you have to start

00:10:31.586 --> 00:10:32.870
really, really young.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:34.491
It was like, okay, you wanna do that,

00:10:34.491 --> 00:10:36.821
you move away from your family.

00:10:36.821 --> 00:10:37.721
- [Kelly] Mm.

00:10:37.721 --> 00:10:39.697
- And you get tutored
on the ice every day.

00:10:39.697 --> 00:10:42.950
And this, I was gonna do pairs skating,

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:45.049
so I would have, so there was another boy,

00:10:45.049 --> 00:10:47.243
he was nine, we were both nine years old.

00:10:47.243 --> 00:10:49.630
I was like, he will
become your everything.

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:52.357
- Wow, it's like an arranged marriage.

00:10:52.357 --> 00:10:53.190
- [Judy] What a commitment.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:54.023
- Like an arranged marriage.

00:10:54.023 --> 00:10:55.630
And then we won't really
know if you're any good

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:59.109
until you're about 14
when you both have gone

00:10:59.109 --> 00:11:03.343
through puberty and we see
if it's all still working.

00:11:03.343 --> 00:11:06.861
- Who would, who says
yes to that opportunity?

00:11:06.861 --> 00:11:07.917
(guests laughing)

00:11:07.917 --> 00:11:09.823
That seems like not a fun time.

00:11:09.823 --> 00:11:10.803
- No, I was like.

00:11:10.803 --> 00:11:11.841
- [Kelly] Yeah, you were like, no.

00:11:11.841 --> 00:11:12.929
- I'm okay.

00:11:12.929 --> 00:11:14.483
- When did you know you wanted to act?

00:11:14.483 --> 00:11:16.569
When did that hit you?

00:11:16.569 --> 00:11:19.283
- I was pretty young. Yeah.

00:11:19.283 --> 00:11:21.777
I was probably about seven or eight.

00:11:21.777 --> 00:11:22.610
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:24.357
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:11:24.357 --> 00:11:26.297
I wrote my parents a letter
saying I wanted to be

00:11:26.297 --> 00:11:28.117
on Ed McMahon's Star Search.

00:11:28.117 --> 00:11:31.983
- Yes. I was in a later
version. (laughing)

00:11:31.983 --> 00:11:33.496
I was in, yeah, American Idol.

00:11:33.496 --> 00:11:34.900
- Yes, yes. You were my dream Kelly.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.190
- I didn't know I wanted to sing though.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.463
Like everybody sang where I grew up,

00:11:37.463 --> 00:11:39.421
so I didn't really know
until I was like a teenager.

00:11:39.421 --> 00:11:40.254
Like I was like 13.

00:11:40.254 --> 00:11:41.087
- [Rachel] Really?

00:11:41.087 --> 00:11:41.920
- Yeah.

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:42.753
And I was just like, and
I knew I liked to sing

00:11:42.753 --> 00:11:43.870
but I didn't know I could
actually do it, you know,

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:44.703
from small town.

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:45.536
- As a job.

00:11:45.536 --> 00:11:47.569
- Yeah. So that's incredible
to know that young.

00:11:47.569 --> 00:11:49.163
You knew very young as well, right?

00:11:49.163 --> 00:11:49.996
- Yeah, I did.

00:11:49.996 --> 00:11:51.048
- You're still young. (laughing)

00:11:51.048 --> 00:11:52.428
- I am. Yes.

00:11:52.428 --> 00:11:55.230
But both my parents are
both actors as well.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.063
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:11:56.063 --> 00:11:57.253
- So I would go into
their auditions with them

00:11:57.253 --> 00:11:59.057
and I would sit on the producer's couch

00:11:59.057 --> 00:12:00.322
and I'd just watch them and be like.

00:12:00.322 --> 00:12:02.277
And then one day when I
was about three and a half,

00:12:02.277 --> 00:12:04.423
I was just like, hey, I wanna do this now.

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:06.940
When can I get an audition?
Please get me with your agent.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.537
- See, you and my daughter.
- Yeah.

00:12:08.537 --> 00:12:09.370
- Yeah.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.763
- So they got me with their agent and

00:12:10.763 --> 00:12:13.181
I went up for a commercial and I got it

00:12:13.181 --> 00:12:15.970
and I had to sing a little
song about Chevrolet.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:17.536
And it was on my fourth birthday

00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:19.036
and I shot it on my fourth birthday.

00:12:19.036 --> 00:12:21.170
So my birthday is my acting anniversary.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:22.763
- Your first paying gig was at four?

00:12:22.763 --> 00:12:23.596
(audience clapping)

00:12:23.596 --> 00:12:24.429
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:12:24.429 --> 00:12:25.262
- [Rachel] I didn't know that. Wow.

00:12:25.262 --> 00:12:26.095
- That's incredible.

00:12:26.095 --> 00:12:26.928
- Yeah.

00:12:26.928 --> 00:12:28.490
- So, Judy, did you
ever wanna' be anything

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:29.443
other than a writer?

00:12:29.443 --> 00:12:30.303
Did you know from a young age?

00:12:30.303 --> 00:12:31.670
- I never wanted to be a writer.

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:32.783
- Wait, what?

00:12:32.783 --> 00:12:35.430
- What? I never knew that
was even a possibility.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:38.088
Never. I loved to read growing up.

00:12:38.088 --> 00:12:38.921
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:12:38.921 --> 00:12:40.903
- But it never occurred
to me that, you know,

00:12:40.903 --> 00:12:44.630
that these people who wrote
the books were living-

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.637
- Off of that, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:12:45.637 --> 00:12:46.470
- real people. No, no.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:47.303
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:12:47.303 --> 00:12:48.136
- No, it never occurred to me.

00:12:48.136 --> 00:12:49.650
- What did you, what
were some of your dreams?

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:50.483
Like, or aspirations?

00:12:50.483 --> 00:12:51.802
- I wanted to be a cowgirl.

00:12:51.802 --> 00:12:52.635
- Okay.

00:12:52.635 --> 00:12:53.468
(Rachel and Abby laughing)

00:12:53.468 --> 00:12:54.301
You can still be one.

00:12:54.301 --> 00:12:55.370
- I can still be one.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.887
And I never rode a horse,
but I had a bicycle.

00:12:57.887 --> 00:12:58.720
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:00.116
- And you know, if that was my-

00:13:00.116 --> 00:13:00.949
- [Kelly] Just call it a horse.

00:13:00.949 --> 00:13:01.782
(horse galloping)

00:13:01.782 --> 00:13:02.615
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:13:02.615 --> 00:13:03.448
- Right.

00:13:03.448 --> 00:13:04.281
- You should, wait, You've
still never rid a horse?

00:13:04.281 --> 00:13:05.114
Now?

00:13:06.288 --> 00:13:07.277
- I know. I've never-

00:13:07.277 --> 00:13:08.690
- Don't say you won't. You should do it.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:11.469
- Pony rides. I had
pony rides in the park.

00:13:11.469 --> 00:13:12.385
- Oh, okay.

00:13:12.385 --> 00:13:14.260
I was gonna say no,
it's an amazing feeling.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:15.093
Yeah.

00:13:15.093 --> 00:13:15.926
- [Judy] Yeah.

00:13:15.926 --> 00:13:16.759
- That's a really cool thing.

00:13:16.759 --> 00:13:18.600
- No, but my stepdaughter
has lots of horses.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:19.433
- Oh, okay.

00:13:19.433 --> 00:13:20.266
- Many horses.

00:13:20.266 --> 00:13:21.099
- [Kelly] She's an equestrian.

00:13:21.099 --> 00:13:21.932
- So I have
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:13:21.932 --> 00:13:22.766
- horses in my family.

00:13:22.766 --> 00:13:24.113
- Okay, hop on one one day.

00:13:24.113 --> 00:13:24.946
(Judy laughing)

00:13:24.946 --> 00:13:25.779
Just saying.

00:13:25.779 --> 00:13:26.612
It's fun. Stay on though.

00:13:26.612 --> 00:13:28.170
I have fallen off and my tailbone.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:30.271
We are here with Rachel McAdams, y'all.

00:13:30.271 --> 00:13:31.298
(audience cheering)

00:13:31.298 --> 00:13:32.259
Abby Ryder Fortson, and Judy Blume.

00:13:32.259 --> 00:13:33.553
The new movie is called

00:13:33.553 --> 00:13:35.280
Are You There God? It's me, Margaret.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.885
It's in theaters tomorrow.

00:13:36.885 --> 00:13:38.532
And there are some points in the movie

00:13:38.532 --> 00:13:40.773
when Abby's character deals
with a group of friends

00:13:40.773 --> 00:13:43.240
that almost feels a
little like Mean Girls.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:44.696
So, Rachel, my favorite thing

00:13:44.696 --> 00:13:47.566
that I say on this show is I love,

00:13:47.566 --> 00:13:48.673
you're one of my favorite
actors of our generation

00:13:48.673 --> 00:13:51.846
because you go from Regina
George to a detective

00:13:51.846 --> 00:13:53.378
to a mom in this movie,

00:13:53.378 --> 00:13:54.960
and you play a wide range of characters,

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.886
which I find interesting.

00:13:56.886 --> 00:13:58.031
Are you purposeful with that?

00:13:58.031 --> 00:14:01.213
Like in choosing what
roles you choose to do?

00:14:01.213 --> 00:14:02.046
- I try to be.

00:14:02.046 --> 00:14:02.946
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:14:02.946 --> 00:14:06.385
- I think it lends to better performance.

00:14:06.385 --> 00:14:07.870
You know, if you're not bored,

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.031
you're not repeating yourself.

00:14:09.031 --> 00:14:09.864
- [Kelly] Yeah, (indistinct)

00:14:09.864 --> 00:14:10.697
- There's, you know, you're like,

00:14:10.697 --> 00:14:11.530
I don't quite understand this.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:12.840
I'm gonna' have to work
really hard to figure it out.

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:13.693
- Yeah.

00:14:13.693 --> 00:14:16.663
- And you know, for me,
variety is the spice of life.

00:14:16.663 --> 00:14:19.093
Like I'm not a creature of habit at all.

00:14:19.093 --> 00:14:19.926
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:14:19.926 --> 00:14:21.305
- Love to go around the
world, see different places.

00:14:21.305 --> 00:14:22.243
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:14:22.243 --> 00:14:23.605
Eat something different every day.

00:14:23.605 --> 00:14:26.706
I'm just, that's just the way I'm geared.

00:14:26.706 --> 00:14:28.246
So, and like you said,

00:14:28.246 --> 00:14:31.613
to get to live many lifetimes in one

00:14:31.613 --> 00:14:33.886
is one of the best things that,

00:14:33.886 --> 00:14:35.344
I don't know if you feel
that way as a writer as well.

00:14:35.344 --> 00:14:36.177
- You do.

00:14:36.177 --> 00:14:37.699
I was just gonna' say
that's, when you're writing,

00:14:37.699 --> 00:14:39.904
you are living, you know,

00:14:39.904 --> 00:14:42.038
you are having all of these experiences

00:14:42.038 --> 00:14:43.560
and you are living other lives.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:44.393
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- [Rachel] Yeah.

00:14:44.393 --> 00:14:46.704
- And in a way it's like acting, you know?

00:14:46.704 --> 00:14:47.537
- Right.

00:14:47.537 --> 00:14:50.386
- Because I, when I was
young, I wanted to be an actor

00:14:50.386 --> 00:14:53.313
but I never trained or did anything, but-

00:14:53.313 --> 00:14:54.146
(Abby laughing)

00:14:54.146 --> 00:14:54.979
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:14:54.979 --> 00:14:58.323
- Writing fulfills that
because I am every character.

00:14:58.323 --> 00:15:00.853
- Mm-hmm. I think writing songs, same way.

00:15:00.853 --> 00:15:01.686
Yeah.

00:15:01.686 --> 00:15:02.697
Even if it's about you,

00:15:02.697 --> 00:15:03.766
it's like different chapters of your life.

00:15:03.766 --> 00:15:04.599
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:15:04.599 --> 00:15:06.298
I think that writing is so therapeutic.

00:15:06.298 --> 00:15:08.425
Is that one of the reasons
why you love to write?

00:15:08.425 --> 00:15:09.653
It's therapeutic for me.

00:15:09.653 --> 00:15:12.880
- It was, it changed my life
and it saved my life and-

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:13.713
- [Kelly] Yeah, me too.

00:15:13.713 --> 00:15:14.580
- came long at just the right time.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:15.413
- Yeah.

00:15:15.413 --> 00:15:18.446
I feel very fortunate 'cause
not everybody has that outlet.

00:15:18.446 --> 00:15:19.486
And I feel very fortunate-

00:15:19.486 --> 00:15:20.319
- Yeah.

00:15:20.319 --> 00:15:21.152
- to have.

00:15:21.152 --> 00:15:21.985
- It was great for me.

00:15:21.985 --> 00:15:22.818
It was-

00:15:22.818 --> 00:15:23.651
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:15:23.651 --> 00:15:24.484
- Absolutely.

00:15:24.484 --> 00:15:25.317
- It's great for us too, it turns out.

00:15:25.317 --> 00:15:26.150
(everyone laughing)

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:26.983
Yeah.

00:15:26.983 --> 00:15:27.816
Thank you as well.

00:15:27.816 --> 00:15:28.780
But we need a break.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.863
We've got more of our,

00:15:29.863 --> 00:15:32.666
Are you there God? It's me,
Kelly, a Judy Blume, oh.

00:15:32.666 --> 00:15:35.153
(heavenly music)

00:15:35.153 --> 00:15:37.560
- [Male] Yes, Kelly. I am here.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.653
You've been calling my
name a thousand times

00:15:39.653 --> 00:15:40.700
during this hour.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.186
You're blowing up my DMs over here.

00:15:42.186 --> 00:15:43.220
(everyone laughing)

00:15:43.220 --> 00:15:44.600
I ain't never heard
people say my name more

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:47.153
in a concentrated period of time.

00:15:47.153 --> 00:15:48.260
Now I'm busy over here looking

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.853
at funny cat videos on Instagram.

00:15:49.853 --> 00:15:50.840
What you want?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:51.673
- Oh my God.

00:15:51.673 --> 00:15:53.580
It's the voice of God,
everybody. You're welcome.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.413
- [Male] That's right. Finally.

00:15:54.413 --> 00:15:55.246
- It's the voice of God.

00:15:55.246 --> 00:15:56.079
- [Male] It finally worked.

00:15:56.079 --> 00:15:57.986
- Well, I'm sorry,

00:15:57.986 --> 00:16:00.653
that's just the title of
our show today, so I didn't,

00:16:00.653 --> 00:16:01.540
so I didn't mean to call you.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:02.373
- [Male] Oh.

00:16:02.373 --> 00:16:03.353
- I mean, I always want you around, man,

00:16:03.353 --> 00:16:05.511
but actually while you're
here, I do have a question.

00:16:05.511 --> 00:16:06.699
- [Male] Sure.

00:16:06.699 --> 00:16:10.153
- Why did you make mosquitoes
and why did people lie

00:16:10.153 --> 00:16:12.319
and say they weren't in
California when they were.

00:16:12.319 --> 00:16:14.173
- [Male] Mosquitoes? Hey,
everybody's gotta eat, right?

00:16:14.173 --> 00:16:15.820
Those are God's little blood suckers.

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:17.477
(everyone laughing)

00:16:17.477 --> 00:16:20.239
We like to call 'em lawyers up here and,

00:16:20.239 --> 00:16:22.660
but I'm really sorry about that.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:23.511
I apologize.
- Yeah.

00:16:23.511 --> 00:16:25.453
- [Male] You know what, from
now on, no more mosquitoes.

00:16:25.453 --> 00:16:26.906
I've eradicated them all.
- Okay, thank you.

00:16:26.906 --> 00:16:27.739
Thank you.

00:16:27.739 --> 00:16:28.572
(audience applauding)

00:16:28.572 --> 00:16:29.405
- [Male] Thanks to you Kelly.

00:16:29.405 --> 00:16:31.266
- Okay, one more question though.

00:16:31.266 --> 00:16:32.218
- [Male] Yes.

00:16:32.218 --> 00:16:34.220
- Do you have anything
you'd want to bestow

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.526
upon our audience today?

00:16:35.526 --> 00:16:36.359
Do you have anything?

00:16:36.359 --> 00:16:37.192
Knowledge? Anything cool?

00:16:37.192 --> 00:16:38.567
- [Male] Well, I do indeed, Kelly.

00:16:38.567 --> 00:16:43.404
It is a special surprise for
everyone here in the audience.

00:16:43.404 --> 00:16:45.881
You are all getting a
pair of tickets to see,

00:16:45.881 --> 00:16:49.661
Are you there God? That's
me. It's me, Margaret.

00:16:49.661 --> 00:16:51.407
In theaters, April 28th.

00:16:51.407 --> 00:16:54.047
(audience cheering)

00:16:54.047 --> 00:16:55.748
- Thank you so much, Lord.

